{
  "id": "dhcp",
  "label": "DHCP",
  "rfc": [
    "2131",
    "2132"
  ],
  "notes": "DHCP over UDP ports 67 and 68. All fixed-offset fields of the 236-byte BOOTP header (RFC 2131 \u00a72) are modelled, including the four payload-embedded IP addresses (host primitives do not reach UDP payload bytes, so they are ipv4 fields) and the client MAC view of chaddr. The variable options region follows at offset 236: the magic cookie (0x63825363, RFC 2132 \u00a72) and the DHCP options, including the message type (option 53), which has no fixed offset. htype is kept as a number: its values come from the IANA ARP parameters (1 = 10Mb Ethernet) and RFC 2131 defines no closed set.",
